Idea:
- Map each username t'an integer id an' build adjacency lists o' mates.
- For each user x: mark all x's mates (an' x itself) in a boolean array.
- For each mate v o' x, loop o'er v's mates w. If w isn't marked, increment cnt[w].
- Track the maximum cnt value mx for x. If mx==0 then x has nowt suggested; else every w with cnt[w]==mx is a suggested mate.
- Reset only the entries ye touched between iterations (we use a cnt vector an' a small list o' touched indices) t'keep it quick.

Complexity:
- Work roughly proportional t'the number o' length-2 paths in t'graph. With m ≤ 5000 this runs reight quick. Memory is linear in number o' users.

